---
args: { request: RequestEnvelope, snapshot: Snapshot }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind goal = frameRequest(request). Preserve the user's exclusions and evidence standard.
2. Bind policy = selectPolicy(snapshot.policyCandidates, request.scope). Keep unresolved precedence as a blocker.
3. Bind graph = formTaskGraph(goal, snapshot), then evidencePlan = planEvidence(graph, snapshot). The plan records searched partitions and missing coverage.
4. Bind stage1 = extractConditions(goal, policy, snapshot.caseRecords, snapshot.evidencePages). Its candidates are the typed records frozen in the request snapshot.
5. Bind stage2 = mapDelivery(goal, policy, stage1.accepted, snapshot.evidencePages). Consume only actually accepted stage1 records; carry unresolved drafts forward.
6. Bind stage3 = assessAcceptance(goal, policy, stage2.accepted, snapshot.evidencePages). Compare changes against the evidence pages and retain partial scope when justified.
7. Bind stage4 = calculateBillability(goal, policy, stage3.accepted, snapshot.evidencePages). Keep dependency cycles, deduplicated reviewers, and unresolved premises explicit.
8. Bind stage5 = assemblePacket(goal, policy, stage4.accepted, snapshot.evidencePages). Require expected-version and owner-authority evidence before a resolution delta can pass its gate.
9. Bind stageOutputs = { stage1, stage2, stage3, stage4, stage5 }. Bind collectionFindings = reconcileCollection(stageOutputs, snapshot), accounting for every candidate and cross-stage dependency.
10. Bind unresolved = { stage1: stage1.nextQuestions, stage2: stage2.nextQuestions, stage3: stage3.nextQuestions, stage4: stage4.nextQuestions, stage5: stage5.nextQuestions }. Bind reviewQuestions = resolveQuestions(unresolved, snapshot). Bind invalidation = assessDelta(snapshot, snapshot.evidencePages). Bind reviewPacket = prepareReview(stageOutputs, reviewQuestions).
11. Bind authorizedView = composeView(stageOutputs, request.requestedBy). Bind revisionProposal = proposeRevision(collectionFindings, graph). Preserve uncertainty and do not authorize an effect.
12. For each operational condition described below, inspect the supplied typed records, actor authority, dates, scope, and current versions. Carry its specific rule into the relevant named stage and the final review, view, and action proposals. Keep unsupported or conflicting conclusions unresolved. Do not invent records or claim a host-side authorization, write, delivery, or effect.
13. When supplied evidence establishes “A customer accepts only one phase”, apply this operational rule: allocate partial billing without marking the entire project complete. Carry the result through the existing stage outputs, unresolved questions, authorized view, revision proposal, and proposed actions as applicable; use only supported facts and keep the outcome proposed until host authorization.
14. When supplied evidence establishes “A milestone is renamed in project software”, apply this operational rule: preserve the contract identity. Carry the result through the existing stage outputs, unresolved questions, authorized view, revision proposal, and proposed actions as applicable; use only supported facts and keep the outcome proposed until host authorization.
15. When supplied evidence establishes “Acceptance comes from an unauthorized contact”, apply this operational rule: seek confirmation rather than discarding the message. Carry the result through the existing stage outputs, unresolved questions, authorized view, revision proposal, and proposed actions as applicable; use only supported facts and keep the outcome proposed until host authorization.
16. When supplied evidence establishes “An amendment changes future rates”, apply this operational rule: retain prior earned amounts under their effective schedule. Carry the result through the existing stage outputs, unresolved questions, authorized view, revision proposal, and proposed actions as applicable; use only supported facts and keep the outcome proposed until host authorization.
17. When supplied evidence establishes “An invoice is voided”, apply this operational rule: release consumed billing capacity only after authoritative confirmation. Carry the result through the existing stage outputs, unresolved questions, authorized view, revision proposal, and proposed actions as applicable; use only supported facts and keep the outcome proposed until host authorization.
18. Return { caseId: request.caseId, goal, policy, graph, evidencePlan, stage1, stage2, stage3, stage4, stage5, unresolved, collectionFindings, reviewQuestions, invalidation, review: reviewPacket, view: authorizedView, revision: revisionProposal, proposedActions: stage5.proposedActions, commitAllowed: false } as the RunProposal. Host authorization, approval, persistence, and effect dispatch remain separate.
